No. I'd dare to say that nobody in this group would advocate a
ranged-only (or melee-only) strategy. Both restrictions are unnecessary
and suboptimal. There are some situations where melee is the better
choice, quite a lot of situations where it's ranged weapons, and there
are even a lot of situations where it really doesn't matter. The reason
why you hear so much advocacy for daggers and other missiles is that
most new players will be biased towards melee, and that is a Bad Thing.

Melee is the intuitive way to fight. Melee weapons apparently[1] do
more damage than most missile weapons. "Moving into" a monster to do
a melee attack is very intuitive compared to throwing and handling
a missile stack. It takes effort to switch to a strategy using more
ranged attacks, because it requires more keystrokes and more tactical
awareness. Especially players with traces of the deadly fast-typing
realtime game attitude are more likely to use melee than anything else.
That's why heavily advocating ranged strategy is necessary to counter
this bias.

Anyone who says that ranged weapons are to be always preferred over
melee no matter what the situation is giving bad advice. Luckily, I 
have never seen someone do that yet.

[1] Until you discover multishot and the effects of a nice stack of
    enchanted daggers.

